From 0d2650a6e765344f50a8002d2baf9cd10765edcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:30:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/26] B70-QSA-T01: one XPU launch-override hook
 (B70_QSA_TUNE) for every QSA Triton kernel

Measurement/tuning only; nothing changes unless an override is set.

- qsa_xpu_tuning.py: B70_QSA_TUNE (JSON or @file) keyed by kernel
  (decode_score, prefill_score, sparse_gqa_decode, sparse_gqa_prefill,
  merge, expand); validated field names; grf_mode passes through as the
  Intel backend launch option; set_overrides() for in-process benches.
  Ignored off XPU (grf_mode is an Intel option).
- The dispatch functions (_decode_launch_config, _prefill_launch_config,
  _select_xpu_config, decode block_n / tiles-per-program) read it, and the
  launch sites and JIT warmups take num_stages / grf_mode from the same
  helpers, so warmup compiles exactly the variant that runs.
- B70_QSA_MIN_DOT_N below 16 is honoured only with
  B70_QSA_ALLOW_SMALL_DOT=1: the arm for Intel triton main, whose frontend
  accepts tl.dot N < 16 (3.8.0+xpu refuses it at compile time).
